  col
    h3 Engage
    h2 NASA Social
    text NASA Social is a program to provide opportunities for NASA’s social media followers to learn and share information about the agency’s missions, people, and programs.
    text NASA Social represents the next evolution of the agency’s social media outreach. Formerly known as NASA Tweetup, the program includes both special in-person events and social media credentials for individuals who meaningfully share NASA news. Through these experiences, NASA Social has brought thousands of people together for unique, behind-the-scenes opportunities centered on exploration and discovery.
    link "Learn More about NASA Social" https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-socials/
  col
    text The Artemis II astronauts speak with invited social media influencers as NASA’s SLS (Space Launch System) rocket and Orion spacecraft roll out to Launch Complex 39B at Kennedy Space Center in Florida on Saturday, Jan. 17, 2026.
    text NASA/Joel Kowsky
